<html><head><style>body{font-family: Arial, sans-serif;} h1{color: #2c3e50;} h2{color: #34495e; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 5px;} pre{background-color: #f4f4f4; padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px;}</style></head><body><h1>Netra-AI: Frontend Integration Guide</h1><p>This document outlines the API endpoints, data payloads, and required UI features that the Frontend Developer needs to build to integrate with the Python backend (<code>visualize_pipeline.py</code>).</p><h2>1. System Architecture</h2><ul><li><b>Backend:</b> Python <code>http.server</code> running on <code>http://localhost:8080</code>.</li><li><b>State Management:</b> The backend manages the Knowledge Graph (<code>entities.json</code>, <code>relationships.json</code>) and the Blockchain Merkle Tree (<code>merkle_tree.json</code>).</li><li><b>Frontend Responsibility:</b> The frontend must handle the live webcam stream, run the <code>face-api.js</code> local AI models to track faces, and send the final names to the backend via REST API.</li></ul><h2>2. Required UI Features</h2><p>The Frontend Developer needs to build the following UI components:</p><ol><li><b>Live CCTV Dashboard:</b> An HTML <code>&lt;video&gt;</code> feed displaying the webcam or local MP4.</li><li><b>Edge AI Face Tracking:</b> Use <code>face-api.js</code> (SSD MobileNet) to draw bounding boxes around faces in the <code>&lt;video&gt;</code> element.</li><li><b>Action Buttons:</b><ul><li><code>[ CAPTURE &amp; SYNC ]</code>: Triggers <code>/api/capture_multi</code>.</li><li><code>[ INGEST WIRETAP ]</code>: Triggers <code>/api/wiretap</code>.</li><li><code>[ RUN PREDICTIVE AI ]</code>: Triggers <code>/api/predict_links</code>.</li></ul></li><li><b>Knowledge Graph View:</b> Use <code>vis-network</code> (or React Flow / D3.js) to render the graph nodes and edges returned by the backend.</li><li><b>Blockchain Banner:</b> A UI element that dynamically displays the updated cryptographic <b>Merkle Root Hash</b> every time an API call is made.</li></ol><h2>3. REST API Documentation</h2><p>The frontend will communicate with the Python backend using standard HTTP POST requests.</p><h3>A. CCTV Capture &amp; Sync</h3><p><b>Endpoint:</b> <code>POST /api/capture_multi</code><br><b>Description:</b> Called when the CCTV camera identifies targets. It updates the graph with <code>SEEN_AT</code> and <code>MET_WITH</code> edges.</p><p><b>Request Payload (JSON):</b></p><pre>{ "targets": [ "Rahul Sharma (PER-001)", "Pedestrian, 34" ] }</pre><p><b>Response Payload (JSON):</b></p><pre>{ "success": true, "nodes": [ { "entity_id": "...", "entity_type": "...", "canonical_name": "..." } ], "edges": [ { "source_id": "...", "target_id": "...", "relationship_type": "SEEN_AT", "evidence_hash": "..." } ], "newRoot": "a4d3f2..." }</pre><p><i>Frontend Action:</i> Add the returned <code>nodes</code> and <code>edges</code> to the graph visualization, and update the Merkle Root banner with <code>newRoot</code>.</p><h3>B. Audio Wiretap Ingestion</h3><p><b>Endpoint:</b> <code>POST /api/wiretap</code><br><b>Description:</b> Simulates ingesting a phone tap. Extracts entities and adds a <code>VOICE_MATCH</code> edge.</p><p><b>Request Payload:</b> None (Empty POST)</p><p><b>Response Payload (JSON):</b></p><pre>{ "success": true, "nodes": [ ... ], "edges": [ { "relationship_type": "VOICE_MATCH", "evidence_hash": "..." } ], "newRoot": "8f9b2c..." }</pre><p><i>Frontend Action:</i> Render an audio-wave animation for 2 seconds to simulate processing, then make the API call. Inject the returned nodes/edges into the graph.</p><h3>C. Predictive Graph AI (Ghost Nodes)</h3><p><b>Endpoint:</b> <code>POST /api/predict_links</code><br><b>Description:</b> Uses backend probability to predict hidden links between existing criminals.</p><p><b>Request Payload:</b> None (Empty POST)</p><p><b>Response Payload (JSON):</b></p><pre>{ "success": true, "edges": [ { "relationship_type": "PROBABLE_ASSOCIATE", "evidence_id": "AI-PREDICTION", "evidence_hash": "AI-PREDICTION-UNVERIFIED" } ] }</pre><p><i>Frontend Action:</i> Inject the returned edges into the graph visualization. Because they are AI predictions (not hard evidence), style these specific edges with <b>dashed lines, yellow color, and a glowing effect</b>.</p></body></html>